  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/designfrontier/WebControl/zipball/v0.3.0",
  "body": "# WebControl 0.3.0\r\n\r\n## Display theme is now a machine setting\r\n- **Moved to Settings ▸ Display.** The Light / Dark / System toggle is gone from the header.\r\n  The choice is stored on the Pi with the other WebControl settings (`uiTheme`), so every\r\n  device shows the same theme.\r\n- **Applies immediately.** Picking a theme switches it at once, with no Save, on every open\r\n  page, without a reload. It can be changed during a job; it doesn't touch the machine or the\r\n  controller's settings.\r\n- **System is the default.** It follows each device's own light or dark mode.\r\n- **No flash on load.** Each browser remembers the last theme it got from the Pi, so a page\r\n  opens in the right theme straight away.\r\n- **A later choice wins.** If you change the theme twice quickly and the first save is refused,\r\n  you keep the later choice.\r\n- **The old per-browser choice** from earlier versions is replaced by the Pi's setting the\r\n  first time the page loads.\r\n\r\n## Header\r\n- **More room for status.** With the theme toggle gone, the status chips keep their longer\r\n  labels at more widths. Landscape iPads still fit the header on one row, and the build commit\r\n  is always shown.\r\n\r\n## Under the hood\r\n- Adds `PUT /api/display/theme` and a `theme` field in `GET /api/state` (contract stays at\r\n  version 4; additive only).\r\n- CI gives the end-to-end test server longer to build when the Rust dependency cache is cold.\r\n\r\n## Install / update\r\nOn the Pi: `webcontrol-update` once this release is published, or install the tarball with its\r\n`install-pi.sh`. Verify downloads against `SHA256SUMS`."
